WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.460
Kicking off the week on Tesla Short's Time, Daily, Episode 496 for June 1st, 2026.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:12.080
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver. Let's see what the new week has in store for Tesla.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:19.380
Tesla's FSD approval in Estonia opens public roads in a third European country after Lithuania

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:25.620
and the Netherlands. Tesla secured approval to operate full self-driving on Estonia's public roads.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.960
This makes Estonia the third European country cleared after Lithuania and the Netherlands.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.760
The approvals follow procedures set by the Dutch Authority, RDW.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.740
Rollout notifications are expected to begin for owners today.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.160
FSD supervised is already rolling out in Lithuania.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.840
Owners with legacy hardware, three computers will not receive the new V14 updates.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.840
The company has shifted to a 99-year-old monthly subscription as the only purchase option

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:01.920
after discontinuing outright sales. While regulatory wins expand, supervised autonomy,

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:08.400
European sales momentum shows parallel demand recovery. Tesla deliveries in Portugal more than

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:14.660
quadrupled compared with May 2025. The increase of lines with similar gains reported earlier

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:20.460
in Norway and France. Britain and Germany are scheduled to release their May registration figures later

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:27.540
this week. The surge came as the overall EV market expanded in the country. Portugal's results show

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:33.760
demand recovery continuing across multiple countries simultaneously. Stock briefly tested moving

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:39.840
averages on the news. Stronger European demand contrasts with internal doubts surfacing inside

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:46.020
Tesla's autonomy team. Current and former members of Tesla's self-driving team have expressed doubts

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:52.460
about relying on the system in critical situations. The internal skepticism centers on the gap between

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:58.160
demonstrated performance and the requirements for unsupervised operation. The report highlights

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:04.580
ongoing challenges in aligning engineering confidence with public claims. Tesla faces a trust problem

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:10.380
inside its own self-driving AI team. Current and former members of the team have voiced doubts about

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.820
depending on the system in life-critical situations. The internal gap between engineering confidence

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:21.580
and public statements remains unresolved. Tesla will need to close that credibility divide before

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:28.660
regulators consider unsupervised operation. Internal engineering skepticism stands in contrast to

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:35.620
steady software refinements reaching owners. CATL plans to begin volume production of sodium ion

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:42.060
cells this year. The initial target range is 600 kilometers. The chemistry is positioned as a

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:48.000
lower cost alternative to current lithium iron phosphate packs. Future versions aim to close the

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.680
energy density gap with entry-level LFP configurations. CATL supplies Tesla and Toyota.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.760
The world's largest battery maker outlined its long-term roadmap,

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:03.500
favoring sodium ion and lithium-air chemistries over solid state approaches.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:09.120
Battery chemistry shifts could eventually support the kind of long-range trips one owner

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:15.900
just completed. Software update 2026.20 introduces a dedicated forward camera view

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:22.620
cleaning panel inside service mode. Technicians can now follow on-screen steps to address a frequent

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:28.140
owner complaint about dirty cameras. The panel guides the process without requiring external

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:34.720
tools or disassembly. The same weekend update adds encryption to dashcam clips stored on the vehicle's

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:40.500
USB drive. Footage is now protected from unauthorized access even if the drive is removed.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:47.200
Owners must enter their Tesla account credentials to view or export the files. Owners can now block

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:52.800
the in-car web browser, Tesla theater, and Tesla arcade directly from vehicle settings.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:59.180
The change gives parents finer control over what children can access while the car is parked or in use.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.860
The feature arrived as part of the broader 2026.20 software package released over the weekend.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:11.520
Everyday software improvements sit alongside dramatic real-world safety demonstrations.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.500
A Model 3 in California fell 300 feet off a cliff yet kept its passengers alive.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:23.580
The incident again demonstrated how Tesla's engineering protects occupants in extreme crashes.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.380
Rescue teams reached the site after the vehicle came to rest at the bottom.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.360
The event underscores the vehicle's structural integrity. This latest example of Tesla

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:41.220
engineering in extreme crashes highlights real durability on a remote cliff. While the Model 3 proved

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:46.920
durability on a remote cliff, another owner pushed a different kind of boundary. An 84-year-old

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:51.860
driver completed the first documented Tesla journey from California to the Arctic Ocean.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:57.740
The trip relied on the vehicle's long-range capability and charging network across remote stretches.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:03.720
The milestone highlights real-world usability of current Tesla models in extreme conditions.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:09.040
Owners' stories of capability lead into competitive pressure from new entrants.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:15.900
Neo introduced a lower-priced model aimed directly at Tesla's volume segment and BYD's offerings.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:22.660
The vehicle targets buyers seeking an affordable electric option with Neo's battery swap infrastructure.

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:28.720
Pricing and specifications positioned it as a direct competitor in the entry-level EV space.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.320
Neo just launched a budget EV to take on Tesla and BYD.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:39.480
Owners' testing recent software changes noted noticeable improvements in response times during

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:45.140
daily driving. The update affects how quickly the vehicle reacts to driver inputs and surrounding

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:51.000
traffic. Feedback so far centers on smoother highway merging and city-street acceleration.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:57.020
A long-term owner reported completing multiple drives without any manual intervention under the latest

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:03.740
FSD version. The account emphasizes consistent performance on familiar routes and changing conditions.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.960
The post reflects growing owner confidence in the supervised system.

